# Copy to .env and `set -a; source .env; set +a` before `uvicorn alpa.api.app:app`
# (or export these in your shell / process manager). Leave unset to run fully
# offline on the deterministic TemplateProvider (no signup, no key, no cost).
#
# Any OpenAI-compatible /chat/completions endpoint works. Pick ONE option below.

# ---- Option A: Groq (free tier, fast, generous limits) ----
# 1. Create a key at https://console.groq.com/keys
# ALPA_LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# ALPA_LLM_API_KEY=gsk_...
# ALPA_LLM_MODEL=llama-3.1-8b-instant

# ---- Option B: Google AI Studio (Gemini, free tier) ----
# 1. Create a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# ALPA_LLM_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai
# ALPA_LLM_API_KEY=AIza...
# ALPA_LLM_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash

# ---- Option C: OpenRouter (many free-tier models, one key) ----
# 1. Create a key at https://openrouter.ai/keys
# ALPA_LLM_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# ALPA_LLM_API_KEY=sk-or-...
# ALPA_LLM_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-3.1-8b-instruct:free

# ---- Option D: Ollama (fully local, zero cost, needs `ollama serve`) ----
# 1. Install https://ollama.com then: ollama pull llama3.1
# ALPA_LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# ALPA_LLM_API_KEY=ollama
# ALPA_LLM_MODEL=llama3.1

# Name the registered provider (used by engine.py's CONTENT_PROVIDER + the
# content pipeline default). Leave as-is unless you register multiple.
ALPA_LLM_PROVIDER=live:v1
